A typical SA is a stochastic recurrence of the form
\begin{align}
    \label{eq:model}
    \theta_{n+1} &= \theta_n + \alpha_n ( f(\theta_n, X_n) + M_{n+1}),
\end{align}
where $\theta_n\in\mathbb{R}^d$ is a vector of parameters, $X_n$ and $M_{n+1}$ are sources of randomness, and $\alpha_n$ is the step-size.

\begin{align}
    \label{eq:model}
    \theta_{n+1} &= \theta_n + \alpha_n ( f(\theta_n, X_n) + M_{n+1}),
\end{align}

